"16 billion": "160 亿",
"infrared detections, searched for anything that moves.": "次红外探测，在其中搜索任何会移动的东西。",
"NASA's NEOWISE telescope photographed every part of the sky about every six months for ten years. We cut the sky into 12,288 equal tiles and, tile by tile, a program links each source's detections across the years, measures how far and how steadily it moves, throws out artefacts, and checks ESA's Gaia catalogue: a mover that Gaia already knows is explained. Then SPHEREx, which mapped the whole sky again in 2025–26, gets a say: the program reads SPHEREx's all-sky spectral cube at the spot where each unexplained mover should be by then, checks that it is there (and gone from where it was in 2014), and takes its 0.75–5 µm spectrum, looking for the methane dip and red colour of a cold brown dwarf. Whatever is left is ranked, so people can look at the most promising candidates first. A candidate is a lead, never a discovery.": "NASA 的 NEOWISE 望远镜用十年时间，大约每六个月拍一遍天空的每个部分。我们把天空切成 12,288 个相同大小的图块，再逐块让程序把每个源在多年间的探测连起来，测量它移动了多远、移动得多稳，剔除伪影，并对照 ESA 的 Gaia 星表：Gaia 已经知道的移动天体就算是已解释的。接着轮到 SPHEREx，它在 2025–26 年又给全天空测绘了一遍：程序在每个未解释移动天体此时应该所在的位置读取 SPHEREx 的全天光谱立方体，检查它是否在那里（并且已不在 2014 年的位置），再取出它 0.75–5 µm 的光谱，寻找冷褐矮星的甲烷吸收凹陷和红色。剩下的会被排序，让人们先看最有希望的候选体。候选体是线索，不是发现。",
"NEOWISE measures the motion (2014–2024). SPHEREx has no source catalogue yet, so the program measures its DR1 cube directly; its ~13″ pixels confirm only fast motions (about 1″ a year or more) and can blend close neighbours.": "NEOWISE 测量运动（2014–2024）。SPHEREx 还没有源星表，所以程序直接测量它的 DR1 立方体；它约 13″ 的像素只能确认快速运动（每年约 1″ 或更多），也可能把靠近的邻居混在一起。",
