"What this search cannot tell you": "这次搜索不能告诉你什么",
"Only the tiles listed here have been searched; the rest of the sky has not been processed yet.": "这里只列出已搜索的图块；天空的其余部分还没有处理。",
"Motions slower than 150 mas per year or faster than 12 arcseconds per year are not searched.": "每年慢于 150 mas 或快于 12 角秒的运动不在搜索范围内。",
"A source must be detected in at least 6 of the roughly 20 WISE visits, so very faint or very red objects near the detection limit can be missed.": "一个源必须在大约 20 次 WISE 巡天中至少 6 次被探测到，所以接近探测极限的很暗或很红的天体可能被漏掉。",
"'Unexplained' means no Gaia DR3 star with a matching motion lies within 3 arcseconds. That is expected for cold brown dwarfs too faint for Gaia, but blends, artefacts next to bright stars and tracks cut at tile edges can look the same.": "“未解释”是指 3 角秒内没有运动匹配的 Gaia DR3 恒星。对于暗到 Gaia 看不到的冷褐矮星，这是正常的，但混合源、亮星旁边的伪影和在图块边缘被截断的轨迹看起来也可能一样。",
"A track that crosses a tile edge is split between the two tiles. When both parts are found and agree in position and motion they are counted once (the longer track is kept); a part too short to be found on its own is lost.": "跨过图块边缘的轨迹会被分到两个图块。如果两部分都被找到，并且位置和运动一致，就只算一次（保留较长的轨迹）；太短而无法单独找到的那一部分会丢失。",
"Motions come from a straight-line fit; parallax is fitted only where a value is given, so very nearby objects can have slightly biased motions.": "运动来自直线拟合；只有给出了数值的地方才会拟合视差，所以非常近的天体，其运动可能有轻微偏差。",
"SPHEREx has no public source catalogue yet; its check measures the all-sky DR1 spectral cube directly at each predicted position. Its pixels are about 13 arcseconds across, so it can only see motions of more than a few pixels over 2014-2026 (roughly 1 arcsecond per year and faster); slower movers can only be shown to be there. Two sources less than a pixel apart are blended, so a spectrum can include a neighbour's light.": "SPHEREx 还没有公开的源星表；它的检查是在每个预测位置直接测量全天 DR1 光谱立方体。它的像素约 13 角秒宽，所以只能看到 2014-2026 年间移动超过几个像素的运动（大约每年 1 角秒及更快）；更慢的移动天体只能证明它在那里。相距不到一个像素的两个源会混在一起，所以光谱可能包含邻居的光。",
"A candidate is not a discovery: each one needs a human check of the images and other catalogues first.": "候选体不是发现：每一个都要先由人检查图像和其他星表。",
"\"Unexplained\" means only that Gaia DR3 has no matching moving star. Many such objects are already known from other surveys (brown dwarfs are too faint and cold for Gaia), and some are artefacts the cuts missed.": "“未解释”只表示 Gaia DR3 没有匹配的移动恒星。许多这样的天体已被其他巡天发现（褐矮星对 Gaia 来说太暗太冷），还有一些是筛选没剔除的伪影。",
"Only people looking at the images, then follow-up observations, can confirm anything new.": "只有人来查看图像，再加上后续观测，才能确认任何新发现。",
"The run's own description of its method": "这次运行对自身方法的说明",
"Each processed tile holds every NEOWISE single-exposure detection from 2014 to 2024 (about 20 million per tile). Detections that fail basic quality cuts (artefact flags, bad frames, moonlight, weak signal) are dropped. WISE scanned each part of the sky about every six months, so the detections of one source in one scan are averaged into a single position per visit. Those positions are linked across the ten years into tracks, including fast movers of up to 12 arcseconds per year, and a straight-line fit gives each track's proper motion and its uncertainty. Tracks seen in at least 6 visits that move at least 150 mas per year with at least 5 sigma are kept as movers. Each mover is compared with Gaia DR3 stars moved to the same date with their own motion. Every mover Gaia does not explain is then looked up in SPHEREx's all-sky spectral cube (data release 1, observed 2025-26): is a source there, where its NEOWISE motion says it should be by then, and gone from where it was in 2014? SPHEREx also gives its 0.75-5 micron spectrum, from which a methane dip at 3.3 microns and a red 3-5 micron colour (signs of a cold brown dwarf) are read as hints. Movers are then ranked: those Gaia does not explain, that are red, that SPHEREx sees where predicted and that have long, clean tracks come first. The top of the list is for people to investigate.": "每个已处理的图块包含 2014 到 2024 年的所有 NEOWISE 单次曝光探测（每个图块约 2000 万个）。没通过基本质量筛选（伪影标记、坏帧、月光、信号弱）的探测会被丢弃。WISE 大约每六个月扫描天空的每个部分，所以一个源在一次扫描中的探测会被平均成每次巡天一个位置。这些位置跨十年连成轨迹，包括每年最高 12 角秒的快速移动天体，再用直线拟合得到每条轨迹的自行及其不确定度。至少在 6 次巡天中被看到、每年至少移动 150 mas、且至少 5 sigma 的轨迹会被保留为移动天体。每个移动天体都会与按各自自行推算到同一日期的 Gaia DR3 恒星比较。Gaia 无法解释的每个移动天体，接着会在 SPHEREx 的全天光谱立方体（第 1 次数据发布，2025-26 年观测）中查找：那里有源吗？它是否在 NEOWISE 的运动所预测的位置，并且已不在 2014 年的位置？SPHEREx 还给出它 0.75-5 微米的光谱，其中 3.3 微米处的甲烷凹陷和 3-5 微米的红色（冷褐矮星的迹象）被当作提示。然后给移动天体排名：Gaia 无法解释、偏红、SPHEREx 在预测位置看到、轨迹又长又干净的排在前面。名单靠前的部分留给人来调查。",
